From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <luke@agent54.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:44:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/50] direct route hardening: browser-allocated images, ready sync token, pipelining

- GuestFrameTextureHost.CreateSource(guest token, size, pool size, webgpu):
  the browser checks ownership and allocates the ring of RGBA shared images
  itself (browser main-thread raster context), exports them to the caller,
  and binds a per-source GuestFrameTextureSourceHost (UniqueReceiverSet,
  dies with the document or the remote). The renderer imports them with
  ImportSharedImage (owning reference in its own channel). Copies are
  requested by slot index, so the renderer can no longer name a mailbox
  the browser would write into.
- CopyNextFrame(index, release token) re-checks ownership per copy, uses a
  per-source wait key, retries twice on an empty result (guest navigated to
  a new process), and replies with the copy's sync token, which the
  VideoFrame waits on.
- The source raises the guest WebContents' capturer count while alive
  (keeps it rendering and composited when hidden; see the next commit).
- Blink: slot state machine (free/copying/ready/held), up to maxInFlight
  (default 2) copies in flight, poolSize default 4, newest ready frame
  handed to read(), release callback posted back to the main thread.
---
